{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528491-bloodstained-love-review","id":1528491,"title":"Bloodstained Love review","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-13T11:45:32-08:00","id":1528491,"title":"Bloodstained Love review","content":"<img width=\"500\" height=\"631\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhtQxrAvb0V0_bExUOlSSnCx5C9vAhO9fswxFu4GhaJ_uARXCkJr5UkkBZ4RrfXGgvTuCJlX-PMZLv_FMQj7JMAEGGcUg4iP2OLF8G8SiUrRaNtze3OussTTYaLN6iFsoSFx6Zh_wpNoUSgQhBd1ppZvou5aVqdbkX-sB5bqEj5IfVvBfY8OVy8GjWEGe6u/s1280/Blood%20Stained%20Love.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhtQxrAvb0V0_bExUOlSSnCx5C9vAhO9fswxFu4GhaJ_uARXCkJr5UkkBZ4RrfXGgvTuCJlX-PMZLv_FMQj7JMAEGGcUg4iP2OLF8G8SiUrRaNtze3OussTTYaLN6iFsoSFx6Zh_wpNoUSgQhBd1ppZvou5aVqdbkX-sB5bqEj5IfVvBfY8OVy8GjWEGe6u/s1280/Blood%20Stained%20Love.jpg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEhtQxrAvb0V0_bExUOlSSnCx5C9vAhO9fswxFu4GhaJ_uARXCkJr5UkkBZ4RrfXGgvTuCJlX-PMZLv_FMQj7JMAEGGcUg4iP2OLF8G8SiUrRaNtze3OussTTYaLN6iFsoSFx6Zh_wpNoUSgQhBd1ppZvou5aVqdbkX-sB5bqEj5IfVvBfY8OVy8GjWEGe6u/s1280/Blood%20Stained%20Love.jpg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> link: <a href=\"https://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2024/01/vampire-masquerade-bloodstained-love.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://unitedfederationofcharles.bl...ined-love.html</a><br /> <br /> BLOODSTAINED LOVE is the latest supplement for VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE and I have to say that it is a supplement I was looking forward to a lot. I admit not entirely for beneficent reasons because my reaction to the premise, &quot;a book about roleplaying love&quot; was basically, &quot;Okay, this will either be awesome or a car crash and I'm there for it either way.&quot; It's horrible but I'm being honest here and you can't tell me some of you weren't thinking the exact same thing. I'm a big fan of storytelling supplements that get into night-to-night elements of Kindred unlife and always liked the OWOD books about things like Elysiums, havens, or how to run your own organized criminal syndicate as a Kindred.<br /> <br /> As stated, the premise is that this book deals with love among the Damned. Do Kindred love? Are they capable of love? How does that love manifest? How do you roleplay that? What are the boundaries? Distilled to its brass tacks, quite a few players want absolutely nothing to do with roleplaying his passionate love affair with Annabelle from Chicago by Night with his Storyteller. Historically, V:TM has also had a significant &quot;creep&quot; factor among LARPs that also casts a pall over the hobby. How would it handle gay, polyarmory, and other issues that V:TM touches on but always seemed afraid to directly address. What about sex? Which, oof.<br /> <br /> This is going to be a pretty long review and is already getting into depth you might not want so the TLDR summary is: the book is okay. In the spectrum between Cults of the Blood Gods (arguably best book ever written for V:TM) and the Second Inquisition (rhymes with &quot;unpster tire&quot;), there's Bloodstained Love. It didn't give me a lot of what I'd hoped for and has a few questionable elements but it's overall a very well-designed sourcebook that strongly emphasizes comfort. Consent too. It gives some basic &quot;romance novel writing 101&quot; tips and hooks that a lot of STs will benefit from. Also, the &quot;should be obvious but isn't&quot; fact that players and STs can make horrifying destructive romances with power imbalances or terrorized partners without making any commentary on themselves in the real world.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, being &quot;okay&quot; is the worst sort of thing to be when doing a review and you didn't come here to hear about me talk about the fact it's mostly basic information about, &quot;Yeah, love triangles are a good source of drama&quot; and &quot;romances across sect lines can have a lot of tension&quot; or even, &quot;The blood bond is artificial and not a true replacement for love.&quot; There's some decent chronicle ideas and advice here that compromises roughly 80% of the book. It's just the remaining 20% really is the stuff worth discussing for better and worse. So take my subsequent discussion of that with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> First to bring up is the book's discussion of &quot;Bleed&quot; which actually isn't a vampire term but a reference to 'bleeding over' emotions from roleplaying. Example: When John Wick's dog dies, you, his player, feel pissed off. This caused a controversy before the book even released as people freaked out about the concept. It's a big deal in Nordic LARP and encouraged while many American (and plenty of other countries too) just noped the hell out of the concept.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think was mostly a cultural translation issue as if you did a find/replace on the discussions with &quot;getting into character&quot;, it would be far less of an issue. However, the book treats bleed as an objective good when it seems to utterly miss the aforementioned &quot;creep&quot; factor that V:TM fandom has always struggled with. When romancing Allicia or Evelyn Stephens from Gary, I'm writing a story with the ST versus trying to get my freak on. Also, I'd hate to be a gamer and suddenly feel like I'm being hit on by a fellow player. Sorry, but it's only Mrs. Phipps who gets to do that and she isn't a gamer.<br /> <br /> Which brings up to problem two and the fact the authors sometimes seem to think this is a lot deeper &quot;method acting&quot; game of INTIMATE DETAIL versus for, what I suspect, 90% of the player it is, a boardgame. Not even improv theater, just a chance to sling some dice and pretend to be Blade or Selene. Allow a single passage here to do all of my explaining for where the author goes wrong in their handling of the subject:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From Page 53:<br /> <br /> IN PORNOGRAPHIC DETAIL<br /> <br /> You can play Vampire in many different contexts, including for the purposes of sexual titillation. One way to do this is to play the game with your sex partner on a one-on-one basis (or with more consenting, informed sex partners), using the sexual exploits of your characters as a form of foreplay </div> </div> </div>Dude. No. Why would you write this? Oversharing much?<br /> <br /> Problem three is the handling of sex and I'm going to put this out there: the sex rules suck. Which is to say only Kindred who have Humanity 7 or above can have sex. It's a stupid rule. It was stupid twenty years ago and it's stupid now. Of anything to change in a supplement about sex, romance, and intimacy--this is the one they should have. David Bowie and Catherine Deneuve were sexually active Kindred in love in The Hunger and they murdered two people a week. The book has Victoria Ash talking at length about her lovers and she's a murderous old elder. They didn't even put in the rule about using the Blush of Life to do it. Physical changes for your Humanity score is stupid and it pisses me off they were left unchanged. Yes, I've put too much thought into this.<br /> <br /> Which is to say this book is also very rules lite. I'm not asking for Dexterity + Performance rules. I'm wondering about &quot;feeding during sex&quot; dangers, frenzy checks for love, alterations to the True Love Merit, blood bond rules, and other things that would actually be interesting during this. There's no Loresheets and only a few Tremere rituals when you'd think there'd be at least a couple of interesting ones related to Romance or Sex. There's some good tables about High vs. Low Humanity dates and gifts but an entire chapter is wasted on NPCs when romantic interest is much better to spark organically among them. Countless players have had their characters love everyone from Lucita to Calebros and it's best to just let interest develop on its own. Any NPC can be a potential LI after all. Sitll, you'd think of all Signature NPCs, Victoria Ash would be statted here.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, my pettiest complaint about this book is probably something only I will be bothered by and that's the portrayal of Victoria Ash. Basically, one section where she talks about the most romantic and fascinating clan before declaring it the Tzimisce. She even discusses her romance with a Fiend. Ha-ha funny subversion. Except, literally one of the few really important character beats of the Toreador Elder is that she was held captive as well as horribly tortured by Tzimisce fleshcraft. It's an event that left her horribly traumatized and terrified of the clan. Now, I know maybe the author doesn't have the kind of lifelong bond with these characters I do. The way some dudes have with Spider-Man or Optimus Prime but this just is especially egregious. Like doing a story about Indiana Jones where you go out of your way to talk about hi lifelong bond with snakes.<br /> <br /> In conclusion, Bloodstained Love is an okay book. It's an enjoyable little conversation piece with a lot of flowery language and some decent ideas for romance stories. Unfortunately, the books falls for its own press a little bit and tries to make the subject a lot more meaningful than it is. It wants to get meaningful and deep when I suspect most of us are quite comfortable keeping it surface level. I give the book credit that it had a good mix of straight, poly, and queer relationships. I also give it credit for lovely art and suggesting that, shock of shocks, players can tell the difference between fiction and reality. It just needed more of the awareness that some players need a bit more in the way of boundaries.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T03:33:26-08:00","id":1528533,"title":"","content":"Man, I'm so not in the target-audience of a book like this one. I can count the times when I dealt with romance as an ST or a player on one hand, so it's hard for me to judge whether this book works or not...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, I think was mostly a cultural translation issue as if you did a find/replace on the discussions with &quot;getting into character&quot;, it would be far less of an issue. However, the book treats bleed as an objective good when it seems to utterly miss the aforementioned &quot;creep&quot; factor that V:TM fandom has always struggled with. When romancing Allicia or Evelyn Stephens from Gary, I'm writing a story with the ST versus trying to get my freak on. Also, I'd hate to be a gamer and suddenly feel like I'm being hit on by a fellow player. Sorry, but it's only Mrs. Phipps who gets to do that and she isn't a gamer. </div> </div> </div>Did you also get this kind of libertine vibe from that Introduction-section of the book? It felt like there was an undertone there that boundaries should get <i>pushed </i>in the name of &quot;exploration&quot;. And it had this bleed-hunting idea of bringing in your own stuff as well, like in that section &quot;Freedom From Fear&quot; or how that section before ends with &quot;What\u2019s the mistake you wish you\u2019d made in your own life if good sense hadn\u2019t stopped you? You can make it in the game instead.&quot;. Since I'm not interested in romantic roleplaying that felt like a really intense suggestion...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Problem three is the handling of sex and I'm going to put this out there: the sex rules suck. Which is to say only Kindred who have Humanity 7 or above can have sex. It's a stupid rule. It was stupid twenty years ago and it's stupid now. Of anything to change in a supplement about sex, romance, and intimacy--this is the one they should have. David Bowie and Catherine Deneuve were sexually active Kindred in love in The Hunger and they murdered two people a week. The book has Victoria Ash talking at length about her lovers and she's a murderous old elder. They didn't even put in the rule about using the Blush of Life to do it. Physical changes for your Humanity score is stupid and it pisses me off they were left unchanged. Yes, I've put too much thought into this. </div> </div> </div>Hmm, the way it read to me is that the book considers blood-drinking to be the central element for sex-scenes when you don't have Humanity 7+. And low-Humanity vampires can still romance other vampires.<br /> <br /> Also, was surprised how pro-&quot;sex scenes should be played out&quot; the book was. At one point, three categories &quot;No Romance&quot;, &quot;Some Romance&quot; and &quot;Full Romance&quot; are mentioned and to me the book read like most of the time the descriptions fell into the category &quot;Full Romance&quot;.<br /> <br /> Some other comments:<ul><li>That &quot;Romance and the Clans&quot;-section on pg 27 was way too short in my opinion (Clans should be a goldmine for introducing various traditions and customs surrounding vampire romance) and the visual design is very confusing. It's all these blurbs of quotes from one vampire commenting on romancing a member of a particular Clan. And the Clans are listed alphabetically. So, for example, it starts with Banu Haquim and you get a quote from a Toreador. The quote is supposed to be about giving a short insight into romancing a Banu Haquim character. But the box the quote is in has the symbol of Clan Toreador. Very confusing arrangement...</li> <li>There's a <i>lengthy </i>section on using TikTok (pg 141-144)... Why?! It even goes into detail on how to use TikTok... No social media platform exists for all eternity and also functionalities, UIs... all of that can change... why would you dedicate this much attention to this...?! Same as with that bit in the Players Guide on online-play... I would completely understand it if it had been put up as a blog-post on the WOD-website (that also helps in keeping the descriptions up-to-date) - but to put it in a book...?!</li> <li>The Merits listed in the book have that caveat of how only ever one Merit can apply in increasing your Humanity and my thought was just &quot;Who cares...?&quot;. If somebody wants to stack the conditions of the Merits with the result that the PC has Humanity 7+ in that situation... why not?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T01:50:13-07:00","id":1536956,"title":"","content":"&quot;Problem three is the handling of sex and I'm going to put this out there: the sex rules suck. Which is to say only Kindred who have Humanity 7 or above can have sex. It's a stupid rule. It was stupid twenty years ago and it's stupid now. Of anything to change in a supplement about sex, romance, and intimacy--this is the one they should have. David Bowie and Catherine Deneuve were sexually active Kindred in love in The Hunger and they murdered two people a week. The book has Victoria Ash talking at length about her lovers and she's a murderous old elder. They didn't even put in the rule about using the Blush of Life to do it. Physical changes for your Humanity score is stupid and it pisses me off they were left unchanged. Yes, I've put too much thought into this.&quot;<br /> <br /> This ain't a Anne Rice novel, or Twilight. It's explicitly stated in VtM cannon that the one, and only, true source of pleasure to a vampire is drinking blood.<br /> <br /> Can they have sex? Yes. To ensnare a victim.<br /> <br /> That said, and again with the pedantics, it's stated in the first 20 pages of any WW splat that you can make the game your own personal universe, with your own personal rules. You're the God, and you can make it whatever you want. You can make vampires who drink blood through their penises and vaginas, if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T10:06:37-07:00","id":1536990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528491-bloodstained-love-review?p=1536956#post1536956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This ain't a Anne Rice novel, or Twilight. It's explicitly stated in VtM cannon that the one, and only, true source of pleasure to a vampire is drinking blood.<br /> <br /> Can they have sex? Yes. To ensnare a victim.<br /> <br /> That said, and again with the pedantics, it's stated in the first 20 pages of any WW splat that you can make the game your own personal universe, with your own personal rules. You're the God, and you can make it whatever you want. You can make vampires who drink blood through their penises and vaginas, if you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anne Rice is where the no sex rule comes from.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T11:03:12-07:00","id":1536993,"title":"","content":"Likewise I'm not part of the target audience for this book as my gaming group views that the most terrifying thing for something to happen for a kindred is falling in love as it's not going to end well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T12:11:01-07:00","id":1537015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528491-bloodstained-love-review?p=1536990#post1536990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anne Rice is where the no sex rule comes from.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Oh, there's blood in the blood book. But you don't want blood; you want sex. And there's no sex in the blood book.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-09T04:42:09-07:00","id":1537073,"title":"","content":"In the context of this book, I don't think insisting on the Humanity 7+ limitation makes a lot of sense. For example, there's this chapter of example NPCs as love-interests. And each character has a section called &quot;Romance&quot; where it goes into detail what trying to flirt with that character and dating them would be like. And then you have story-seeds for romantic scenes and what potential relationship-complications look like.<br /> <br /> Here is an excerpt of what sort of tone this book strikes. This is from Layla Trivera's Romance-section, a freshly turned Tremere: &quot;Her style of flirting is clumsy because she\u2019s not particularly good at hiding her interest in someone. When she has a crush, it\u2019s painfully obvious as she tries to get closer to the object of her interest, complimenting them awkwardly.<br /> <br /> Initially, the biggest obstacle to romance with Layla is that she believes she must make sense of her situation and find a stable status quo before she can date anyone. She doesn\u2019t want to be a liability to more experienced Kindred, or someone\u2019s project. She wants to love as equals and that means she has to improve her situation.<br /> <br /> Yet at the same time, the heart wants what it wants, even if it no longer beats.&quot;<br /> <br /> Or this is how the romance-section for Condor, a Ventrue Neonate in the Camarilla, starts: &quot;Condor is\u2026 a fuckboy.<br /> <br /> Were it not for his feeding preferences, Condor loves sex. He is a suave, uncontrollable flirt, and spends many nights a week pursuing sexual conquests. It helps that he has managed to cultivate his Humanity successfully enough that he can enjoy mortal sex.<br /> <br /> Condor goes for men of all types: young inexperienced twinks fresh out of college. Older leather-daddies with decades of experience. Gymbunnies who look good but don\u2019t really know what to do. Nerdy gays with cosplay fetishes. \u201cNot my type\u201d doesn\u2019t really exist in his vocabulary. If you\u2019re a man who has reasonable game, chances are Condor will take you home for a tumble on his couch.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> This book is less concerned with VtM canon and more with describing a type of roleplaying experience where it's really <i>all </i>about romance and sex. This is for a VtM-game where the stakes revolve around making a relationship work and maintaining it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T12:52:28-07:00","id":1537212,"title":"","content":"Then I'm most defintely not part of the target group for this book in any form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T13:31:12-07:00","id":1537213,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's important to note that this book is only relevant for a V5 game if you and your group care <i>deeply </i>about romantic roleplay. This book gets quite intense at times in what it talks about those topics. Just take the two excerpts I posted previously. This book expects STs to roleplay that. Is that something you can envision being part of your game? If the answer is no, then this book is not for you. This book isn't really an add-on to V5, it's more a resource for a certain special interest aka for those people who like this kind of intense romantic/sexual roleplaying.<br /> <br /> I can see a book like Blood Sigils being useful for groups even if the game isn't all about Blood Sorcery but this book...? Forget about Session Zero, this one would require even more prep. And of course, one of the issues of this book is that it was written with this uncritical portrayal of Bleed-hunting (the deliberate pursuit of experiencing Bleed). It was only due to the backlash that they then released a separate free online document with a more sober take on Bleed and how to handle that.<br /> <br /> If you're not super-interested in exploring romance and sex in your roleplaying-sessions, this book isn't for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T14:02:00-07:00","id":1537215,"title":"","content":"Yes I'm not big on Blood Sorcery either as it's not my favorite Discipline as it comes dead last after Dominate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T14:14:04-07:00","id":1537216,"title":"","content":"Anne Rice's sexless vampires is, ironically, a result of her emphasis on sensuality. Her vampires love looking at each other, running their fingers through each other's silky hair, and generally are attracted to each other in a way that blurs the line between sexual and the love of art. Essentially, AnneRicepires mostly love each other the way one loves owning a statue, and the way one loves owning a magnificent horse. They very much crave beautiful companions despite their sexlessness.<br /> <br /> It's a hard thing to roleplay, and a hard thing to convey to the normies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 06-12-2024, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-11T15:44:01-07:00","id":1537232,"title":"","content":"I haven't read her stuff in years and I really don't feel a strong desire either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-13T23:18:09-07:00","id":1549285,"title":"","content":"I recently picked up a copy of this because (a) it may be of use in a project I will be working on for the Storytellers Vault and (b) the shop I was purchasing it from had a 50% discount on the volume, versus the 10% they normally offer (which is a little suggestive. I am amazed by just how padded this book is, frequently using a page for a concept, when a paragraph might suffice. And the love interests? I have never come across a collection of characters which have been quite so deserving of being burnt to death in a warehouse fire...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-17T09:26:08-07:00","id":1549395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528491-bloodstained-love-review?p=1536990#post1536990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anne Rice is where the no sex rule comes from.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also simply storytelling logic: if a vampire loses their heartbeat but gains Cool Blood Magic, it takes a little something extra to sell the notion of The Curse being a bane and not a blessing un-disguised.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-24T14:37:27-07:00","id":1550365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1528491-bloodstained-love-review?p=1549395#post1549395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also simply storytelling logic: if a vampire loses their heartbeat but gains Cool Blood Magic, it takes a little something extra to sell the notion of The Curse being a bane and not a blessing un-disguised.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, while true, it's not like vampires haven't had the sexual element from the entire time. Them being hedonists is more interesting than them being corpses.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the curse is they kill people.<br /> <br /> Being eternally celibate seems a weird new line to draw in the sand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T04:26:47-07:00","id":1550375,"title":"","content":"Not celibate, sexless: that\u2019s not the same thing, since celibacy is a choice and being completely unable to experience sexual arousal unless you\u2019re bleeding someone to death is an Actual Curse.<br /> <br /> Also, and I may be rather cynical when I say this, a curse that merely requires you to kill people from time to time is exactly the sort of thing gamers (and other genre fans) will shrug off with \u201cWell, so long as they\u2019re the <i>wrong</i> sort of people\u2026\u201d whilst a curse that makes you as horny as a Ken doll might actually<br /> make them wonder if trading your humanity for cool vampire powers is worth the exchange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-25T16:17:35-07:00","id":1550387,"title":"","content":"That's because you're looking at it as if the <b>players</b> should feel cursed, not the character.<br /> <br /> Vampire's curse is a trope, a narrative device. <b>I hope</b> everyone here agrees that being forced to hurt, possibly kill, other humans is a curse.<br /> <br /> More than that, the vampire as an archetype is a monster, a predator, <b>specially a sexual predator</b>. While in many ways the Blood thing is a metaphor for sex, it is part and parcel of the genre that sometimes there's no metaphor.<br /> <br /> While there's room for the assexual monster, the vampire is an extremely sexual monster in the genre, and has always been.<br /> <br /> And as far as it applies for the game, the game isn't about making the <b>players</b> feel they're cursed at all costs. If a player buys into the personal horror side of the game, they do just fine. If they don't, incapacitating their fictional penises won't make them &quot;play the game right&quot;. Some people are in it for the power fantasy <i>and that is fine</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-28T09:05:22-07:00","id":1550443,"title":"","content":"(Well I\u2019m not saying that VAMPIRE players are Wrong and Bad and probably aggressively-casual about bleeding random people to death, but I\u2019ve just finished Season 5 of WHAT WE DO IN THE SHADOWS and may be projecting certain frustrations with Guillermo* onto VAMPIRE players \u2026).<br /> <br /> <br /> *<i>Dangit, the boy just refuses to CHOOSE when he has the potential to be the next Peter Cushing and ample, ample evidence that vampires are, on the whole, quite horrible people</i>.<br /> <br /> <i>The Sunk Cost Fallacy is a horrible, horrible thing</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}